{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An attached macro emits a small record into a section LinkerSets owns, and a typed run-time API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enumerates every record of one kind in a deterministic order. Each record carries a kind, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clients share the mechanism without seeing each other’s records. Failures are typed errors; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run-time API never traps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A declaration registers itself with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", tagged with a kind: four ASCII","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters read as a 32-bit integer. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" of that kind finds every such declaration","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at run time:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import LinkerSets","","enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}","","let routes = LinkerSet<Route>(kind: LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)).values"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A client that registers one kind of thing can give it a macro with the kind fixed, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from its own compiler plugin. The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"schema